080d26fd2c3be1e401bae1a6b339b62f28f4abbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevenzg/aiga/commits/080d26fd2c3be1e401bae1a6b339b62f28f4abbd"}],"sha":"667bdc7918ee3013e74febc462a03db713800a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevenzg/aiga/commits/667bdc7918ee3013e74febc462a03db713800a38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6308804?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stevenzg","id":6308804,"login":"stevenzg","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYzMDg4MDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stevenzg","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevenzg/aiga/commits/080d26fd2c3be1e401bae1a6b339b62f28f4abbd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-10T19:49:46Z","email":"steven.zg@outlook.com","name":"Steven"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-10T19:49:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: initial Aiga micro-frontend framework implementation (#2)\n\n* feat: implement Aiga micro-frontend framework with adaptive sandbox architecture\n\nCore framework implementing the design document''s five innovations:\n\n1. Adaptive Sandbox Architecture - four isolation tiers (none/light/strict/remote)\n   with different browser primitives and cost/isolation trade-offs\n2. iframe Pool with LRU eviction - pre-creates hidden iframes at startup for\n   near-instant (~0ms) sandbox activation instead of 50-100ms on-demand creation\n3. Service Worker Resource Layer - centralized cache management across iframe\n   boundaries with cache-first, network-first, and stale-while-revalidate strategies\n4. Overlay Layer Proxy - detects and teleports modal/popover/dropdown elements\n   outside Shadow DOM for correct viewport-relative positioning and z-index\n5. Type-safe RPC Communication - request/response pattern over postMessage with\n   Promise-based returns, auto serialization, and timeout handling\n\nUnified API via <mf-app> Web Component that works in any framework.\nShadowRealm-ready adapter abstraction for future migration.\n\nIncludes example app embedding React and Svelte apps side by side.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* feat: complete all five design document innovations\n\nFills all implementation gaps identified in design doc audit:\n\n1. Light sandbox: Add window Proxy isolation (proxy-window.ts) that\n   traps property writes to a local scope, preventing globals leakage.\n   Redirects document.body operations to Shadow DOM container.\n\n2. Strict sandbox: Add DOM Proxy bridge (dom-bridge.ts) that injects\n   an interceptor script into same-origin iframes to detect overlay\n   elements (modal/popover) and report them to the host overlay layer.\n\n3. Keep-alive: Add KeepAliveManager with priority-based LRU eviction\n   (high/normal/low), maxAlive enforcement, auto-promotion after N\n   visits, and lifecycle events (keep-alive-start, keep-alive-restore).\n\n4. Smart prewarming: Add Prewarmer with route adjacency analysis,\n   navigation frequency tracking, transition pattern prediction, and\n   idle-time resource prefetching via <link rel=\"prefetch\">.\n\n5. SW semver negotiation: Add version registry that tracks requested\n   dependency versions across iframes, finds the highest backward-\n   compatible version per package, and rewrites URLs at fetch time.\n\n6. RPC typed proxies: Add useMicroApp<T>(), useShell<T>(), and\n   exposeApi() helpers that wrap RpcChannel in a Proxy for type-safe\n   contract-driven communication that feels like local function calls.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: comprehensive code review — security, leak, and correctness fixes across 17 files\n\nCRITICAL fixes:\n- postMessage wildcard origin → derive origin from app.src URL (strict, remote, channel, dom-bridge)\n- RPC proxy thenable infinite loop → NON_PROXIED_KEYS blocks ''then''/''catch''/''finally''\n- Light sandbox executeScripts now actually uses proxy window via scoped Function()\n- Auto-resize listener leaks → tracked in Maps, cleaned up on unmount/destroy\n- Async lifecycle serialization → Promise chain prevents mount/unmount races\n- Duplicate Shadow DOM render → ''rendered'' flag prevents reconnect duplication\n- Remote sandbox security → removed allow-same-origin from iframe sandbox attribute\n- Keep-alive eviction → onEvict callback properly destroys evicted iframes\n\nHIGH fixes:\n- Proxy-window body identity → cached body proxy prevents multiple wrapper creation\n- deleteProperty returns true for non-local properties (strict mode compliance)\n- Singleton config → warns when getInstance called with config after init\n- Pool overflow → logs warning, shrinks on release when exceeding maxSize\n- Pool reset → restores default sandbox attributes on iframe reuse\n- Overlay observer → disconnects previous observer before creating new one\n- Cleanup observers tracked → Set of MutationObservers, all disconnected on dispose\n- SW redundant state → rejects promise instead of hanging forever\n\nMEDIUM fixes:\n- Serializable type → removed undefined (not JSON-serializable)\n- RpcMessage → proper discriminated union with typed message interfaces\n- Strict destroy order → saves iframe ref before unmount, then pool.remove\n- Prewarmer cleanup → tracks <link> elements, removes from DOM on dispose\n- DOMParser for HTML injection → replaces innerHTML in none.ts and light.ts\n- Adapters cleared on dispose\n- SW tsconfig → excludes register.ts (main-thread file, not worker)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: second-pass review — keepAlive lifecycle, origin validation, overlay bridge\n\nCRITICAL:\n- strict.ts/remote.ts: keepAlive unmount now preserves iframe reference\n  instead of destroying it; mount reuses existing iframe on restore\n  without re-navigating (preserves iframe state)\n- strict.ts destroy: properly cleans up iframe tracking after unmount\n\nHIGH:\n- getOrigin/deriveOrigin: throw on invalid URL instead of silently\n  falling back to wildcard ''*'' (strict.ts, remote.ts, channel.ts)\n- none.ts: unmount selector uses app.id instead of app.name\n  (prevents wrong-element removal with duplicate names)\n- dom-bridge: overlay handler now calls overlayLayer.addOverlayFromHtml()\n  to actually process detected cross-iframe overlays\n- overlay-layer.ts: added public addOverlayFromHtml() method for\n  cross-iframe bridge integration\n- Cache config: standardized across index.ts and aiga.ts to require\n  explicit cache config object with enabled !== false\n\nMEDIUM:\n- remote.ts: extracted cleanupListeners() to eliminate DRY violation\n  between unmount/destroy (was ~30 duplicated lines)\n- light.ts/none.ts: listener cleanup tracked per-app via\n  listenerCleanups Map, cleaned up in unmount to prevent leaks\n- worker.ts: added runtime type validation for SW message data\n  (precache urls, evict url, register-version package/version)\n\nLOW:\n- proxy.ts exposeApi: type cast includes Promise<Serializable>\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: third-pass review — XSS, listener leaks, lifecycle race, origin validation\n\nCRITICAL:\n- overlay-layer.ts: replaced innerHTML with DOMParser in addOverlayFromHtml\n  (prevents XSS from cross-iframe bridge HTML)\n- strict.ts/remote.ts: tracked onLoad listener in setupAutoResize via\n  loadListeners Map; cleaned up on unmount to prevent memory leaks\n\nHIGH:\n- mf-app.ts: captured inKeepAlive state atomically before queuing in\n  lifecycleLock to prevent race between connect/disconnect callbacks\n- mf-app.ts: removed duplicate OverlayLayer creation for light sandbox\n  (adapter creates its own; MfAppElement only creates for strict)\n\nMEDIUM:\n- strict.ts/remote.ts: added origin validation to resize message handler\n  (was missing, unlike RPC messages which validate origin)\n- pool.ts: added disposed check in release() to prevent operating on\n  destroyed pool\n- prewarmer.ts: fixed scheduling starvation — don''t cancel pending idle\n  callback on rapid navigation; let it complete\n- light.ts/none.ts: added onerror handlers for external script loading\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: address test plan gaps — security, overlays, routing, timeouts, props\n\nMajor fixes based on test plan gap analysis (44 failing/missing cases):\n\nSecurity (SEC-01/02, JS-06):\n- Bridge script overrides window.top/parent to prevent iframe escape\n- localStorage/sessionStorage namespaced per app via Proxy in bridge\n- Overlay heuristic tightened: position:fixed alone no longer triggers (OV-13)\n\nOverlay system (OV-01~07):\n- Iframe promotion approach: iframe goes full-viewport when overlay active\n- Overlays maintain full interactivity (clicks, scroll, animations)\n- Bridge detects overlay show/hide and sends messages to host\n- Strict sandbox CSS adds .aiga-promoted class for viewport mode\n\nCSS variable sync (CSS-03, CSS-06):\n- Strict mode: CSS vars sent to iframe via postMessage after load\n- Bridge script receives __aiga_css_vars and applies to :root\n- Light mode: MutationObserver on documentElement for reactive updates\n- Both modes observe style/class attribute changes on :root\n\nTimeouts and error handling (ERR-01, ERR-03, ERR-04):\n- Load timeout via Promise.race in mf-app mount() (default 10s)\n- RPC timeout configurable (default 10s, was hardcoded 30s)\n- Error boundary in light/none sandboxes (window error/unhandledrejection)\n- CORS error detection in light/none fetch with helpful message\n\nProxy window fixes (JS-10, DOM-03):\n- Timer tracking: setTimeout/setInterval/rAF IDs tracked in Sets\n- revoke() clears all tracked timers automatically on unmount\n- document.title writes scoped per sandbox (don''t leak to host)\n\nProps system (RPC-13):\n- props property on <mf-app> element (Record<string, unknown>)\n- Props sent to sub-app via RPC ''props-update'' event on mount\n- Props re-sent on keep-alive restore\n- Setting props triggers immediate RPC emit if channel active\n\nRouter (NAV-01~09):\n- New Router class with history and hash mode support\n- Route matching with dynamic params (:id) and wildcards (*)\n- Nested route support with match chain\n- Route guards (beforeEach, per-route beforeEnter)\n- 404 handling with configurable fallback\n- <mf-router-view> web component for declarative routing\n- Back/forward navigation via popstate/hashchange listeners\n\nConfig additions:\n- AigaConfig.loadTimeout (default 10_000ms)\n- AigaConfig.rpcTimeout (default 10_000ms)\n- AppInstance.props field\n- MfAppConfig.props field\n- Aiga.loadTimeout/rpcTimeout getters\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: second-round audit — cookie isolation, route matching, overlay detection\n\n- SEC-02: Add document.cookie namespace isolation in dom-bridge (strict)\n  and proxy-window (light) sandboxes\n- Add origin validation for bridge postMessage handler\n- Fix nested route matching with proper matchPrefix() method\n- Re-sync iframe height after overlay demotion in strict sandbox\n- Watch attribute changes (class/role/style) in overlay-layer for\n  deferred overlay detection by UI libraries\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: third-round audit — dead code, router bugs, CSS observer restore\n\n- Remove dead OverlayLayer from mf-app.ts (strict now uses iframe promotion)\n- Clear load timeout timer on successful mount to prevent resource leak\n- Fix router navigate() to parse query from path argument instead of\n  stale window.location.search\n- Fix hash mode: use pushState instead of location.hash to prevent\n  duplicate hashchange → onUrlChange processing\n- Re-create CSS variable observer on keep-alive restore in strict sandbox\n  (unmount cleans it up, restore needs to re-establish it)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* feat: add documentation site with Fumadocs\n\nLanding page with:\n- Hero section with code snippet\n- Adaptive sandbox tier cards\n- Feature grid (9 capabilities)\n- Comparison table vs qiankun/micro-app/wujie/Module Federation\n- Architecture diagram\n- CTA section\n\nDocumentation pages:\n- Introduction & quick start\n- Motivation: why Aiga was built\n- Detailed comparison with alternatives\n- Getting started guide with step-by-step instructions\n- Sandbox tiers deep dive (none/light/strict/remote)\n- RPC channel API reference\n- Router guide (nested routes, guards, hash mode)\n- Overlay handling (teleportation vs iframe promotion)\n- Test scenarios: 93 test cases across 14 categories\n\nInteractive demos:\n- Sandbox tier explorer with capability matrix\n- RPC channel simulator with message log\n- Router playground with live route matching\n- Overlay handling visualization (light vs strict)\n\nBuilt with Next.js 16 + Fumadocs v16 + Tailwind CSS v4.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix(docs): correct test count (91 not 93) and remove unused comparison fields\n\n- test-scenarios.mdx: fix \"93 scenarios across 14 categories\" → \"91 scenarios across 12 categories\"\n- landing page: remove unused strategy/overhead fields from comparisons array\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* docs: update root README with full project documentation\n\nAdd comprehensive README covering architecture, features, quick start,\nrouting, RPC, comparison table, project structure, and development guide.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: critical RPC setup for strict sandbox, router hash query parsing\n\n- Fix setupRpc() unable to find iframe in strict sandbox — querySelector\n  can''t pierce the nested Shadow DOM boundary, so adapters now set\n  app.iframe during mount for direct access\n- Fix router onUrlChange() losing query params in hash mode — query\n  was read from window.location.search (empty in hash mode) instead\n  of being parsed from the hash fragment path\n- Fix rpc-ready event firing for none/light sandboxes where no RPC\n  channel exists, which was misleading to consumers\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* refactor: rename mf-app → aiga-app, mf-router-view → aiga-view; full-width docs\n\nRename all custom element tags, classes, types, and CSS across source code,\ndocumentation, landing page, demos, and README. Make docs layout full-width\nby overriding --fd-layout-width.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* feat(docs): add live demo page with real cross-framework sub-apps\n\nNew \"Live Demo\" page under Interactive section shows two independently\ndeployed apps (React + Svelte) running side by side in Aiga''s strict\nsandbox with pooled iframes, status indicators, and pool stats.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: iframe height propagation for cross-origin strict/remote sandboxes\n\nCross-origin iframes can''t auto-resize (bridge script injection and\nResizeObserver both fail). Add height:100% through the full chain\n(aiga-container → shadow host → wrapper → iframe) so the iframe fills\nits container when auto-resize is unavailable. Same-origin auto-resize\nstill overrides via inline style.height.\n\nAlso update live-demo to use responsive viewport-based height.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix(docs): build library before docs so dist/aiga.js exists on Vercel\n\nThe live demo imports from ../../dist/aiga.js which is gitignored.\nAdd build:lib step that installs root deps and builds the library\nbefore next build, so Vercel deployments work without dist in git.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix(docs): build library before dev server too\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* feat(docs): add 3 interactive demo scenarios with React + Svelte sub-apps\n\nAdd tabbed live demo page with cross-framework communication scenarios:\n- Cross-app Text Sync: React editor → Svelte preview via RPC\n- Shared Counter: React buttons → Svelte display with visual bar\n- Shared Todo List: React todo manager → Svelte list with progress stats\n\nEach scenario pairs a React sub-app (left) with a Svelte sub-app (right),\nrunning in sandbox=\"strict\" iframes with host-mediated RPC relay.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: resolve relative URLs in sandbox/RPC; split demos into separate pages\n\n- Fix `new URL(url)` → `new URL(url, window.location.href)` in strict.ts,\n  remote.ts, and rpc/channel.ts so relative paths like `/demos/foo.html` work\n- Split tabbed live demo into 4 separate pages:\n  - Cross-Origin Apps (Vercel URLs)\n  - Text Sync (React editor → Svelte preview)\n  - Shared Counter (React buttons → Svelte display)\n  - Shared Todos (React manager → Svelte list)\n- Refactor live-demo.tsx: shared useAiga hook, individual exports per demo\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* chore: update fumadocs generated source maps for new demo pages\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix(docs): use 70vh height for cross-origin demo iframes\n\nCross-origin iframes can''t auto-resize (no bridge injection), so give\nthe Rosetta apps more vertical space instead of the fixed 420px.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: class name mismatch breaking iframe height chain\n\nThe rename from mf-app to aiga-app missed the CSS class names on\nDOM elements. The CSS targeted .aiga-container/.aiga-loading/.aiga-error\nbut elements still had class mf-container/mf-loading/mf-error.\nThis broke height:100% propagation — the iframe fell back to min-height\ninstead of filling its container.\n\nAlso add height:100% to the strict adapter''s host div to complete\nthe height chain from <aiga-app> through to the iframe.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"30b8920d817c3b591c100e7b3448021b04518b55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevenzg/aiga/git/trees/30b8920d817c3b591c100e7b3448021b04518b55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stevenzg/aiga/git/commits/080d26fd2c3be1e401bae1a6b339b62f28f4abbd","verification":{"payload":"tree 30b8920d817c3b591c100e7b3448021b04518b55\nparent 388570d3b64f3b34307b04702be20fcfa7a286a7\nauthor Steven <steven.zg@outlook.com> 1770752986 +1300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770752986 +1300\n\nfeat: initial Aiga micro-frontend framework implementation (#2)\n\n* feat: implement Aiga micro-frontend framework with adaptive sandbox architecture\n\nCore framework implementing the design document''s five innovations:\n\n1. Adaptive Sandbox Architecture - four isolation tiers (none/light/strict/remote)\n   with different browser primitives and cost/isolation trade-offs\n2. iframe Pool with LRU eviction - pre-creates hidden iframes at startup for\n   near-instant (~0ms) sandbox activation instead of 50-100ms on-demand creation\n3. Service Worker Resource Layer - centralized cache management across iframe\n   boundaries with cache-first, network-first, and stale-while-revalidate strategies\n4. Overlay Layer Proxy - detects and teleports modal/popover/dropdown elements\n   outside Shadow DOM for correct viewport-relative positioning and z-index\n5. Type-safe RPC Communication - request/response pattern over postMessage with\n   Promise-based returns, auto serialization, and timeout handling\n\nUnified API via <mf-app> Web Component that works in any framework.\nShadowRealm-ready adapter abstraction for future migration.\n\nIncludes example app embedding React and Svelte apps side by side.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* feat: complete all five design document innovations\n\nFills all implementation gaps identified in design doc audit:\n\n1. Light sandbox: Add window Proxy isolation (proxy-window.ts) that\n   traps property writes to a local scope, preventing globals leakage.\n   Redirects document.body operations to Shadow DOM container.\n\n2. Strict sandbox: Add DOM Proxy bridge (dom-bridge.ts) that injects\n   an interceptor script into same-origin iframes to detect overlay\n   elements (modal/popover) and report them to the host overlay layer.\n\n3. Keep-alive: Add KeepAliveManager with priority-based LRU eviction\n   (high/normal/low), maxAlive enforcement, auto-promotion after N\n   visits, and lifecycle events (keep-alive-start, keep-alive-restore).\n\n4. Smart prewarming: Add Prewarmer with route adjacency analysis,\n   navigation frequency tracking, transition pattern prediction, and\n   idle-time resource prefetching via <link rel=\"prefetch\">.\n\n5. SW semver negotiation: Add version registry that tracks requested\n   dependency versions across iframes, finds the highest backward-\n   compatible version per package, and rewrites URLs at fetch time.\n\n6. RPC typed proxies: Add useMicroApp<T>(), useShell<T>(), and\n   exposeApi() helpers that wrap RpcChannel in a Proxy for type-safe\n   contract-driven communication that feels like local function calls.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: comprehensive code review — security, leak, and correctness fixes across 17 files\n\nCRITICAL fixes:\n- postMessage wildcard origin → derive origin from app.src URL (strict, remote, channel, dom-bridge)\n- RPC proxy thenable infinite loop → NON_PROXIED_KEYS blocks ''then''/''catch''/''finally''\n- Light sandbox executeScripts now actually uses proxy window via scoped Function()\n- Auto-resize listener leaks → tracked in Maps, cleaned up on unmount/destroy\n- Async lifecycle serialization → Promise chain prevents mount/unmount races\n- Duplicate Shadow DOM render → ''rendered'' flag prevents reconnect duplication\n- Remote sandbox security → removed allow-same-origin from iframe sandbox attribute\n- Keep-alive eviction → onEvict callback properly destroys evicted iframes\n\nHIGH fixes:\n- Proxy-window body identity → cached body proxy prevents multiple wrapper creation\n- deleteProperty returns true for non-local properties (strict mode compliance)\n- Singleton config → warns when getInstance called with config after init\n- Pool overflow → logs warning, shrinks on release when exceeding maxSize\n- Pool reset → restores default sandbox attributes on iframe reuse\n- Overlay observer → disconnects previous observer before creating new one\n- Cleanup observers tracked → Set of MutationObservers, all disconnected on dispose\n- SW redundant state → rejects promise instead of hanging forever\n\nMEDIUM fixes:\n- Serializable type → removed undefined (not JSON-serializable)\n- RpcMessage → proper discriminated union with typed message interfaces\n- Strict destroy order → saves iframe ref before unmount, then pool.remove\n- Prewarmer cleanup → tracks <link> elements, removes from DOM on dispose\n- DOMParser for HTML injection → replaces innerHTML in none.ts and light.ts\n- Adapters cleared on dispose\n- SW tsconfig → excludes register.ts (main-thread file, not worker)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: second-pass review — keepAlive lifecycle, origin validation, overlay bridge\n\nCRITICAL:\n- strict.ts/remote.ts: keepAlive unmount now preserves iframe reference\n  instead of destroying it; mount reuses existing iframe on restore\n  without re-navigating (preserves iframe state)\n- strict.ts destroy: properly cleans up iframe tracking after unmount\n\nHIGH:\n- getOrigin/deriveOrigin: throw on invalid URL instead of silently\n  falling back to wildcard ''*'' (strict.ts, remote.ts, channel.ts)\n- none.ts: unmount selector uses app.id instead of app.name\n  (prevents wrong-element removal with duplicate names)\n- dom-bridge: overlay handler now calls overlayLayer.addOverlayFromHtml()\n  to actually process detected cross-iframe overlays\n- overlay-layer.ts: added public addOverlayFromHtml() method for\n  cross-iframe bridge integration\n- Cache config: standardized across index.ts and aiga.ts to require\n  explicit cache config object with enabled !== false\n\nMEDIUM:\n- remote.ts: extracted cleanupListeners() to eliminate DRY violation\n  between unmount/destroy (was ~30 duplicated lines)\n- light.ts/none.ts: listener cleanup tracked per-app via\n  listenerCleanups Map, cleaned up in unmount to prevent leaks\n- worker.ts: added runtime type validation for SW message data\n  (precache urls, evict url, register-version package/version)\n\nLOW:\n- proxy.ts exposeApi: type cast includes Promise<Serializable>\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: third-pass review — XSS, listener leaks, lifecycle race, origin validation\n\nCRITICAL:\n- overlay-layer.ts: replaced innerHTML with DOMParser in addOverlayFromHtml\n  (prevents XSS from cross-iframe bridge HTML)\n- strict.ts/remote.ts: tracked onLoad listener in setupAutoResize via\n  loadListeners Map; cleaned up on unmount to prevent memory leaks\n\nHIGH:\n- mf-app.ts: captured inKeepAlive state atomically before queuing in\n  lifecycleLock to prevent race between connect/disconnect callbacks\n- mf-app.ts: removed duplicate OverlayLayer creation for light sandbox\n  (adapter creates its own; MfAppElement only creates for strict)\n\nMEDIUM:\n- strict.ts/remote.ts: added origin validation to resize message handler\n  (was missing, unlike RPC messages which validate origin)\n- pool.ts: added disposed check in release() to prevent operating on\n  destroyed pool\n- prewarmer.ts: fixed scheduling starvation — don''t cancel pending idle\n  callback on rapid navigation; let it complete\n- light.ts/none.ts: added onerror handlers for external script loading\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: address test plan gaps — security, overlays, routing, timeouts, props\n\nMajor fixes based on test plan gap analysis (44 failing/missing cases):\n\nSecurity (SEC-01/02, JS-06):\n- Bridge script overrides window.top/parent to prevent iframe escape\n- localStorage/sessionStorage namespaced per app via Proxy in bridge\n- Overlay heuristic tightened: position:fixed alone no longer triggers (OV-13)\n\nOverlay system (OV-01~07):\n- Iframe promotion approach: iframe goes full-viewport when overlay active\n- Overlays maintain full interactivity (clicks, scroll, animations)\n- Bridge detects overlay show/hide and sends messages to host\n- Strict sandbox CSS adds .aiga-promoted class for viewport mode\n\nCSS variable sync (CSS-03, CSS-06):\n- Strict mode: CSS vars sent to iframe via postMessage after load\n- Bridge script receives __aiga_css_vars and applies to :root\n- Light mode: MutationObserver on documentElement for reactive updates\n- Both modes observe style/class attribute changes on :root\n\nTimeouts and error handling (ERR-01, ERR-03, ERR-04):\n- Load timeout via Promise.race in mf-app mount() (default 10s)\n- RPC timeout configurable (default 10s, was hardcoded 30s)\n- Error boundary in light/none sandboxes (window error/unhandledrejection)\n- CORS error detection in light/none fetch with helpful message\n\nProxy window fixes (JS-10, DOM-03):\n- Timer tracking: setTimeout/setInterval/rAF IDs tracked in Sets\n- revoke() clears all tracked timers automatically on unmount\n- document.title writes scoped per sandbox (don''t leak to host)\n\nProps system (RPC-13):\n- props property on <mf-app> element (Record<string, unknown>)\n- Props sent to sub-app via RPC ''props-update'' event on mount\n- Props re-sent on keep-alive restore\n- Setting props triggers immediate RPC emit if channel active\n\nRouter (NAV-01~09):\n- New Router class with history and hash mode support\n- Route matching with dynamic params (:id) and wildcards (*)\n- Nested route support with match chain\n- Route guards (beforeEach, per-route beforeEnter)\n- 404 handling with configurable fallback\n- <mf-router-view> web component for declarative routing\n- Back/forward navigation via popstate/hashchange listeners\n\nConfig additions:\n- AigaConfig.loadTimeout (default 10_000ms)\n- AigaConfig.rpcTimeout (default 10_000ms)\n- AppInstance.props field\n- MfAppConfig.props field\n- Aiga.loadTimeout/rpcTimeout getters\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: second-round audit — cookie isolation, route matching, overlay detection\n\n- SEC-02: Add document.cookie namespace isolation in dom-bridge (strict)\n  and proxy-window (light) sandboxes\n- Add origin validation for bridge postMessage handler\n- Fix nested route matching with proper matchPrefix() method\n- Re-sync iframe height after overlay demotion in strict sandbox\n- Watch attribute changes (class/role/style) in overlay-layer for\n  deferred overlay detection by UI libraries\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: third-round audit — dead code, router bugs, CSS observer restore\n\n- Remove dead OverlayLayer from mf-app.ts (strict now uses iframe promotion)\n- Clear load timeout timer on successful mount to prevent resource leak\n- Fix router navigate() to parse query from path argument instead of\n  stale window.location.search\n- Fix hash mode: use pushState instead of location.hash to prevent\n  duplicate hashchange → onUrlChange processing\n- Re-create CSS variable observer on keep-alive restore in strict sandbox\n  (unmount cleans it up, restore needs to re-establish it)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* feat: add documentation site with Fumadocs\n\nLanding page with:\n- Hero section with code snippet\n- Adaptive sandbox tier cards\n- Feature grid (9 capabilities)\n- Comparison table vs qiankun/micro-app/wujie/Module Federation\n- Architecture diagram\n- CTA section\n\nDocumentation pages:\n- Introduction & quick start\n- Motivation: why Aiga was built\n- Detailed comparison with alternatives\n- Getting started guide with step-by-step instructions\n- Sandbox tiers deep dive (none/light/strict/remote)\n- RPC channel API reference\n- Router guide (nested routes, guards, hash mode)\n- Overlay handling (teleportation vs iframe promotion)\n- Test scenarios: 93 test cases across 14 categories\n\nInteractive demos:\n- Sandbox tier explorer with capability matrix\n- RPC channel simulator with message log\n- Router playground with live route matching\n- Overlay handling visualization (light vs strict)\n\nBuilt with Next.js 16 + Fumadocs v16 + Tailwind CSS v4.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix(docs): correct test count (91 not 93) and remove unused comparison fields\n\n- test-scenarios.mdx: fix \"93 scenarios across 14 categories\" → \"91 scenarios across 12 categories\"\n- landing page: remove unused strategy/overhead fields from comparisons array\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* docs: update root README with full project documentation\n\nAdd comprehensive README covering architecture, features, quick start,\nrouting, RPC, comparison table, project structure, and development guide.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: critical RPC setup for strict sandbox, router hash query parsing\n\n- Fix setupRpc() unable to find iframe in strict sandbox — querySelector\n  can''t pierce the nested Shadow DOM boundary, so adapters now set\n  app.iframe during mount for direct access\n- Fix router onUrlChange() losing query params in hash mode — query\n  was read from window.location.search (empty in hash mode) instead\n  of being parsed from the hash fragment path\n- Fix rpc-ready event firing for none/light sandboxes where no RPC\n  channel exists, which was misleading to consumers\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* refactor: rename mf-app → aiga-app, mf-router-view → aiga-view; full-width docs\n\nRename all custom element tags, classes, types, and CSS across source code,\ndocumentation, landing page, demos, and README. Make docs layout full-width\nby overriding --fd-layout-width.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* feat(docs): add live demo page with real cross-framework sub-apps\n\nNew \"Live Demo\" page under Interactive section shows two independently\ndeployed apps (React + Svelte) running side by side in Aiga''s strict\nsandbox with pooled iframes, status indicators, and pool stats.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: iframe height propagation for cross-origin strict/remote sandboxes\n\nCross-origin iframes can''t auto-resize (bridge script injection and\nResizeObserver both fail). Add height:100% through the full chain\n(aiga-container → shadow host → wrapper → iframe) so the iframe fills\nits container when auto-resize is unavailable. Same-origin auto-resize\nstill overrides via inline style.height.\n\nAlso update live-demo to use responsive viewport-based height.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix(docs): build library before docs so dist/aiga.js exists on Vercel\n\nThe live demo imports from ../../dist/aiga.js which is gitignored.\nAdd build:lib step that installs root deps and builds the library\nbefore next build, so Vercel deployments work without dist in git.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix(docs): build library before dev server too\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* feat(docs): add 3 interactive demo scenarios with React + Svelte sub-apps\n\nAdd tabbed live demo page with cross-framework communication scenarios:\n- Cross-app Text Sync: React editor → Svelte preview via RPC\n- Shared Counter: React buttons → Svelte display with visual bar\n- Shared Todo List: React todo manager → Svelte list with progress stats\n\nEach scenario pairs a React sub-app (left) with a Svelte sub-app (right),\nrunning in sandbox=\"strict\" iframes with host-mediated RPC relay.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: resolve relative URLs in sandbox/RPC; split demos into separate pages\n\n- Fix `new URL(url)` → `new URL(url, window.location.href)` in strict.ts,\n  remote.ts, and rpc/channel.ts so relative paths like `/demos/foo.html` work\n- Split tabbed live demo into 4 separate pages:\n  - Cross-Origin Apps (Vercel URLs)\n  - Text Sync (React editor → Svelte preview)\n  - Shared Counter (React buttons → Svelte display)\n  - Shared Todos (React manager → Svelte list)\n- Refactor live-demo.tsx: shared useAiga hook, individual exports per demo\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* chore: update fumadocs generated source maps for new demo pages\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix(docs): use 70vh height for cross-origin demo iframes\n\nCross-origin iframes can''t auto-resize (no bridge injection), so give\nthe Rosetta apps more vertical space instead of the fixed 420px.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n* fix: class name mismatch breaking iframe height chain\n\nThe rename from mf-app to aiga-app missed the CSS class names on\nDOM elements. The CSS targeted .aiga-container/.aiga-loading/.aiga-error\nbut elements still had class mf-container/mf-loading/mf-error.\nThis broke height:100% propagation — the iframe fell back to min-height\ninstead of filling its container.\n\nAlso add height:100% to the strict adapter''s host div to complete\nthe height chain from <aiga-app> through to the iframe.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Jfw51kxoTArNe9uas537pc\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpi4vaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8ikQAFxLXZqOgoNLGEDRy+sX/ySG\ny8Jdcfe94UH9A/qDJngsb+RbS6AY8GI1+9gPOa9jkgs0ux7xNnip1q0VVjxC8PjH\noKV285G9y3FjlQRpg0W8+kXrtiE/5lAxNkAxFeeCSwaZVnapm3oFYR7f2xLmzAtK\n9xqiwP4gcvRmi8OPHxSiKap3h+uzGwNFiRe0s4u0In04krgHPGHne22L9hympoqp\n5S1ZnNqePZumzQ5imtiGScj6m+QSw30+ZOC1Imqq2l2FKKPEj2COZL4JlqcM9MCc\nUP8rw1Uvy5PASOEQozN5vGPfPmI+Ruhh83GnwGB+o1duALaPqsFcjkRvlMSXWpyR\nXiWh8bcaynd9/XHMx3dV8l9XDJoQZzuQz29VKrEFSqeiyd/LrWzJm6OQpzEBgtDB\nCYXDcNOyilsNn2SRRq3VF6he1A77DrfyeiE7pCHEGkMUDMkbTo560sL0HG91dukd\nAJDZOLZGUmRMKiv8YhsqDMw6E+/pEXMtDB6PePtTjgYf0gZJgouRRCFy2w6LurAb\nvruXkzkuKXfX2KpqdscjuzI/RCGDJHphwojIwlREJrO0zUhdEUu9Uzg2zYF6rYie\nNvZN0v/Rd2SzoJDeZrm5Pcl7yZohcuQ2KndUocOVPa/NqiibWu6TLM8q81qNuWBC\nGnFPFXomHqhV974Wfyw4\n=0P0n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-10T19:49:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com