"type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/2361aec9f01e0cee59af555a71e10d21d5b89f94/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:29:07Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T14:29:07Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(security): laboratory routes refuse malformed documents with one sentence, never exception text\n\nThe replay, background-job and cohort routes returned str() of caught\nKeyError and TypeError as the 422 message, so a missing field echoed the\ncaller''s key name (''problem'', ''cohort'') and a wrong type echoed Python\ntype detail. An integer where a document was expected raised an uncaught\nAttributeError and answered HTTP 500.\n\nstudio/api/fits.py now defines the fixed MALFORMED_DOCUMENT sentence, the\nstructural fault set (LookupError, TypeError, AttributeError), the full\nset a laboratory route refuses with 422, and refusal_message(), which\nkeeps a ValueError''s text and replaces every structural fault. The sync\nreplay route and the four catches plus the error helper in fit_jobs.py\nuse them.\n\nTests: five malformed replays through the real app (the default test\nclient raises server errors, so a 500 fails), the refusal_message\ncontract, and six malformed documents over the job, cohort and replay\nroutes asserting the exact detail, no key or type text and no submitted\njob; they fail against the previous handlers. Independent second-eye\nreview: CLEAR on the exact patch.\nParity: Python-only Studio surface. Benchmarks: no benchmarked path.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: 56e9","tree":{"sha":"fbdc79f55838ac60a2302c918438a9fd8a87257e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/fbdc79f55838ac60a2302c918438a9fd8a87257e"},"url":"https://api.github.com