"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T00:58:08Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(hygiene): the pre-commit workflow passes on main again\n\nThe push of 2ad4560d5 turned the Pre-commit workflow red on three hooks,\nfor changes that had never been run through pre-commit locally:\n- end-of-file-fixer: accel/mojo/kernels/qcfs.mojo lacked its final newline.\n- typos: SB_RAM40_4KNW (a Lattice iCE40 primitive), the Verilog port\n  `dout` in the synthesis test designs and the deliberately misspelt\n  label \"trian\" in a training-config refusal test are allowlisted in\n  .typos.toml with their reason; \"mis-shaped\" in the conversion loss\n  report''s docstring reads \"malformed\" (API reference regenerated).\n- go-doc-ratchet: 14 exported Go declarations had landed undocumented\n  (conversion and loaders tests and two package clauses). Each now says\n  what it checks; debt is 1529, one below the old ceiling, and the\n  ceiling follows it down.\n`pre-commit run --all-files` passes locally; go vet and go test pass for\nthe conversion and loaders packages.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"eecf9c1f4ff862738d66f8bb9107d916e4825ef1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/eecf9c1f4ff862738d66f8bb9107d916e4825ef1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/7ea802fae5a356a2caaf94f4b96e443bb310b971","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/7ea802fae5a356a2caaf94f4b96e443bb310b971","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDdlYTgwMmZhZTVhMzU2YTJjYWFmOTRmNGI5NmU0NDNiYjMxMGI5NzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/2ad4560d58a67ffb26d52139b21a31864ec2622f","sha":"2ad4560d58a67ffb26d52139b21a31864ec2622f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/2ad4560d58a67ffb26d52139b21a31864ec2622f"}],"sha":"7ea802fae5a356a2caaf94f4b96e443bb310b971","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/7ea802fae5a356a2caaf94f4b96e443bb310b971"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/2ad4560d58a67ffb26d52139b21a31864ec2622f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T00:39:00Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T00:39:00Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"feat(studio): frequency response as gain and phase about an operating point; a physiological ODE template\n\nFrequency response (a metric-contract change, stated in the contract):\n- It drove a mean-zero sine, amplitude · sin(2πft), and reported the mean\n  rate alone; the current changed sign every half cycle and the Studio''s\n  default model left its safety bounds under it, so the action failed.\n- The drive is now bias · (1 + depth · sin 2πft): the run''s current is the\n  operating point, depth 0.5 by default and below 1, so the current never\n  changes sign. From the spike times over the largest whole number of\n  drive cycles it reports, per frequency, the mean rate, the rate''s first\n  harmonic 2|Σ exp(−2πi f t_k)| / window, the gain (per unit of modulating\n  current), the phase by which the rate lags the drive, and the vector\n  strength. A frequency without one whole cycle in the run is reported as\n  not measured (null, domain partial), not estimated from a fraction.\n- A request that still sends `amplitude` is refused with that reason; a\n  zero bias is refused. The sine protocol takes an optional `bias` on both\n  run paths (validated, stated in the model receipt only when set, so no\n  existing receipt changes).\n- The view is a Bode plot (gain above, phase lag below, log frequency\n  axis); its screen-reader description and table give every column and\n  mark unmeasured frequencies. The Studio asks for frequencies from the\n  one that fits two whole cycles in the run up to 200 Hz, and refuses a\n  zero current instead of inventing an operating point.\n- Measured on ATypeK (1000 ms, bias 10): rates 357-372 Hz, gain 32-43 Hz\n  per unit, no failure. Estimator tests use spike trains with known\n  answers (peaks: vector strength 1, lag 0°; troughs: ±180°).\n\nODE template:\n- The LIF template (tau_m 10 ms, C 1) put v_inf at +35 mV and fired about\n  590 Hz at the Studio''s default 10 (1670 Hz at the server template''s 30).\n  It is now tau_m 20 ms, C 10 pF (R = 2 GΩ, I in pA): rheobase 7.5 pA,\n  about 36 Hz at 10 pA (measured: 0 Hz at 7.5, 18 at 8, 36 at 10, 71 at\n  15); the server template''s current is 10. The \"Threshold Behavior\"\n  preset uses the same cell, so its ramp to 15 crosses the rheobase\n  halfway (first spike near 120 ms) instead of at once.\n\nAlso:\n- tests/test_studio_router_contract.py pinned 140 routes and failed on\n  main since the fit and cohort job routes and the target-profiles route\n  landed (148); the count is raised with the reason, the fit_jobs module\n  is listed, and the committed OpenAPI reference is regenerated.\n- The protocol table in the Studio guide said four protocols (there are\n  five, sine was missing), described the pulse train as 5 ms on/off (it is\n  five pulses per run at a fifth duty) and the step as on for the last\n  80 % (it is on from 20 % to 80 %).\n- Regenerated: docs/API_REFERENCE.md, the capability manifest, snapshot\n  and README block (one more test file).\n- Gates: every tests/test_studio*.py plus related suites, 4386 passed; the\n  six Julia event-runtime tests failed only for want of the CI-provisioned\n  PYTHON_JULIACALL_* variables and pass (13) with them; vitest 1381, e2e\n  14/30/2/7/1; whole-package mypy --strict (1721 files), bandit, ruff and\n  ruff format over the tree, SPDX, capability, benchmark evidence gate.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"aeb31b04c6306e0e4e7c678dc80638a44ab06b41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/aeb31b04c6306e0e4e7c678dc80638a44ab06b41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/2ad4560d58a67ffb26d52139b21a31864ec2622f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/2ad4560d58a67ffb26d52139b21a31864ec2622f","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDJhZDQ1NjBkNThhNjdmZmIyNmQ1MjEzOWIyMWEzMTg2NGVjMjYyMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/38ee3d74279679cddcf1aef53a513e1bea921c29","sha":"38ee3d74279679cddcf1aef53a513e1bea921c29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/38ee3d74279679cddcf1aef53a513e1bea921c29"}],"sha":"2ad4560d58a67ffb26d52139b21a31864ec2622f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/2ad4560d58a67ffb26d52139b21a31864ec2622f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/38ee3d74279679cddcf1aef53a513e1bea921c29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:26:34Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:26:34Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): a refused share or model link stays said when the startup simulation begins\n\n- The live suite failed on \"#model=NoSuchNeuron\": the Playwright trace\n  shows the catalogue load (36.78 s), the link refused into `error`, the\n  default model selected, and its automatic simulation starting at\n  37.78 s; every run''s start patch sets error to null, so the message\n  vanished before anyone could read it. It survives only when the run\n  starts first; the same test passed in every earlier run today.\n- The refusal is now `linkNotice`, a store field no run clears, shown in\n  its own alert banner with a Dismiss button.\n- New store test: a refused link, then the start of a simulation; the\n  notice is still there and `error` is untouched.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"93600724b033122b810608a03da93ea2a759ff84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/93