llowing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/e5bcd8e2eb792ea02108e805044067da03d23c2e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:26:33Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T23:26:33Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): a pipeline stopped at synthesis says why, with Yosys''s own error or the network size that ran out of time\n\n- A failed synthesis left the pipeline result without an error, so the\n  canvas said \"Pipeline failed at synthesise: unknown\"; the default\n  100-neuron network, whose synthesis runs past the 60 s limit, ended\n  that way.\n- The pipeline now stops at \"synthesise\" with a sentence: a timed-out\n  run (the synthesis result carries timed_out) names the network''s size\n  and says whether it fits the target device is unknown; synthesis time\n  grows quickly with size (measured: 10 neurons 17 s, 20 neurons 58 s).\n  Any other failure carries Yosys''s message.\n- That message was the last 500 characters of the log, which after a\n  command error is the pass''s help text; it is now Yosys''s ERROR lines\n  (found anywhere in a line: its standard output can end mid-line).\n- The 60 s limit is SYNTHESIS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS; capacity_device_name()\n  names the judged device. Tests run real Yosys, stopped by a shortened\n  limit and failed by an unknown synth_ice40 option.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"2cd68eefea634922dfd7311dd6e8295666937abb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/2cd68eefea634922dfd7311dd6e8295666937abb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/e5bcd8e2eb792ea02108e805044067da03d23c2e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/e5bcd8e2eb792ea02108e805044067da03d23c2e","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGU1YmNkOGUyZWI3OTJlYTAyMTA4ZTgwNTA0NDA2N2RhMDNkMjNjMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/1bcd1cecd32cd7abee05021355f9168ecbb70360","sha":"1bcd1cecd32cd7abee05021355f9168ecbb70360","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/1bcd1cecd32cd7abee05021355f9168ecbb70360"}],"sha":"e5bcd8e2eb792ea02108e805044067da03d23c2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/e5bcd8e2eb792ea02108e805044067da03d23c2e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/1bcd1cecd32cd7abee05021355f9168ecbb70360/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:55:07Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:55:07Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): the workbench and status bar name the run in progress instead of calling every run a simulation\n\n- The Studio has one busy flag for every run: simulation, analyses,\n  characterisation, compile, synthesis, network simulation and the\n  network pipeline. The workbench''s simulation card read it as\n  \"Simulation is running\" and the status bar as \"simulating...\", so a\n  pipeline or an f-I sweep was reported as a simulation.\n- Each run''s start patch now also sets busyWith: the view it fills\n  (\"f-I curve\", \"A/B compare\", from the panel titles), \"Simulation\",\n  \"Characterization\", \"Compilation\", \"FPGA synthesis\", \"FPGA synthesis for\n  every target\", \"Network simulation\" or \"Network pipeline\". The status\n  bar says \"<run> running…\"; the simulation card says Running only for a\n  simulation and otherwise \"Waiting: <run> is running; a simulation can\n  start when it ends\".\n- Nullclines now start on the phase-plane view they fill, so their run is\n  named for it.\n- Also: e0361700c (\"document the state layer\") inserted the comment \"An event\n  source that is driven by the cases rather than by a network.\" 21 times;\n  one documents the fake event source in studioTrainingStream.test.ts,\n  the other twenty sat inside object literals and between unrelated\n  functions (compiler, model selection, operator workbench, synthesis and\n  training store tests). Those twenty are removed; no code changes.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"0544690bb5771b86a54d04fac5586c68a2191c12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/0544690bb5771b86a54d04fac5586c68a2191c12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/1bcd1cecd32cd7abee05021355f9168ecbb70360","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/1bcd1cecd32cd7abee05021355f9168ecbb70360","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDFiY2QxY2VjZDMyY2Q3YWJlZTA1MDIxMzU1ZjkxNjhlY2JiNzAzNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/7d6afddfbba935c2d3c5f4712d3a8d2522ccce0b","sha":"7d6afddfbba935c2d3c5f4712d3a8d2522ccce0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/7d6afddfbba935c2d3c5f4712d3a8d2522ccce0b"}],"sha":"1bcd1cecd32cd7abee05021355f9168ecbb70360","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/1bcd1cecd32cd7abee05021355f9168ecbb70360"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/7d6afddfbba935c2d3c5f4712d3a8d2522ccce0b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:42:41Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:42:41Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): the side-by-side panel is a named section with a named group and a visible limit\n\n- The final audit of every view found each catalogue model name twice\n  among the checkboxes: the side-by-side panel''s list had no group name\n  and its title was a styled div, so a screen reader heard two identical\n  unnamed lists beside the multi-model picker''s \"Models to overlay\".\n- It is now an h2 \"Side-by-side (n of 4)\" with a group named \"Models to\n  compare side by side\"; once four are chosen the other boxes are disabled\n  instead of a fifth click being silently ignored, as in the multi-model\n  picker.\n- Final pass on the landed tree: the audit (23 views, four viewports)\n  found no low contrast, unnamed control, horizontal overflow or console\n  error; nine of ten live actions pass. The tenth, frequency response on\n  the default ATypeK model, leaves the safety bounds under a mean-zero\n  sine: the definition of the stimulus is an open owner decision.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"4d63a0ebc6ee5ead398d7e3ecd236564348e7971","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/4d63a0ebc6ee5ead398d7e3ecd236564348e7971"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/7d6afddfbba935c2d3c5f4712d3a8d2522ccce0b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/7d6afddfbba935c2d3c5f4712d3a8d2522ccce0b","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDdkNmFmZGRmYmJhOTM1YzJkM2M1ZjQ3MTJkM2E4ZDI1MjJjY2NlMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/76fa4aea3b4d7326eae13b50e4337e043e99d747","sha":"76fa4aea3b4d7326eae13b50e4337e043e99d747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/76fa4aea3b4d7326eae13b50e4337e043e99d747"}],"sha":"7d6afddfbba935c2d3c5f4712d3a8d2522ccce0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/7d6afddfbba935c2d3c5f4712d3a8d2522ccce0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/76fa4aea3b4d7326eae13b50e4337e043e99d747/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:28:17Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T22:28:17Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): FPGA resources are counted from each family''s primitives and judged against a named device\n\n- Measured on one design (256x16 memory, 16x16 multiplier, 24-bit counter),\n  Yosys 0.33: the substring counter was right for iCE40 only. ECP5 read\n  0 LUTs (12 CCU2C carry cells are 24 LUT4) and 0 block RAM (DP16KD);\n  Gowin counted 3096 LUTs (wide MUX2_LUT5-8 multiplexers) and 64 block\n  RAMs (RAM16SDP4 LUT-RAM), a false \"does not fit\"; SB_MAC16 would never\n  have counted as a DSP. Each family now has a table of what its\n  primitives take; ECP5 now matches nextpnr-ecp5 exactly (24 LUT4, 56 FF,\n  1 DP16KD, 1 MULT18X18D).\n- Only the design''s modules are counted; Yosys also writes the family''s\n  cell library, whose timing cells inflated \"cells\" and \"wires\".\n- A cell of unknown cost (ECP5/Gowin distributed RAM, a hand-placed\n  primitive) is listed in uncounted_cells and leaves fits_device null\n  unless the counted cells already overflow: the counts are then a floor.\n- The Xilinx target failed on every design: synth_xilinx has no \"-json\"\n  option. Netlists are written with write_json (synth_gowin -json also\n  withheld block RAM for nextpnr-gowin, which the target does not run),\n  and synth_xilinx flattens so the top module holds every cell.\n- Capacities: ECP5 LFE5U-25F is 24288 LUT4/FF as nextpnr reports (the\n  table said 24576); the Gowin row matched no device and is now GW2A-18\n  (20736 LUT4, 15552 FF, 46 B-SRAM, 48 multipliers, DS102); Xilinx is the\n  XC7A35T in RAMB18 halves (100). Every verdict carries capacity_device,\n  and the FPGA view names it, says a fit is by count (placement and\n  routing decide the rest), says an estimate is an estimate, and says\n  when it cannot judge.\n- Docs: supported-targets tables in the dashboard guide, the Studio index\n  and the compression tutorial; counting and sources explained.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"11268589a7e26b24b401686a05297a52b75b127f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/11268589a7e26b24b401686a05297a52b75b127f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/76fa4aea3b4d7326eae13b50e4337e043e99d747","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/76fa4aea3b4d7326eae13b50e4337e043e99d747","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDc2ZmE0YWVhM2I0ZDczMjZlYWUxM2I1MGU0MzM3ZTA0M2U5OWQ3NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/f995a8523b3a099ac6c6c87b598b8d70f4c6e0af","sha":"f995a8523b3a099ac6c6c87b598b8d70f4c6e0af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/f995a8523b3a099ac6c6c87b598b8d70f4c6e0af"}],"sha":"76fa4aea3b4d7326eae13b50e4337e043e99d747","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/76fa4aea3b4d7326eae13b50e4337e043e99d747"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/f995a8523b3a099ac6c6c87b598b8d70f4c6e0af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T21:58:44Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T21:58:44Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): a synthesised design is judged against its device; the pipeline no longer calls an overflowing network complete\n\n- Measured: a two-population network of 20 neurons synthesised to 6237\n  LUTs for the 5280-LUT iCE40 UP5K and the pipeline reported \"Pipeline\n  complete\"; the resource bar printed \"(100.0%)\" because the share was\n  capped with the bar. (The default 100-neuron network times out at 60 s.)\n- Synthesis and estimate results carry fits_device and exceeds_capacity\n  (needed and available per resource; no verdict for a target without\n  capacity data). The pipeline stops at a \"fit\" step with a sentence naming\n  what the design needs and what the device has.\n- iCE40 capacity said 0 DSPs; the UP5K has 8 SB_MAC16 blocks (Lattice iCE40\n  UltraPlus Family Data Sheet), so a design with one multiplier would have\n  been judged not to fit.\n- FPGA view: the real share with \"over capacity\", and a fit verdict line for\n  a synthesis and for an estimate. Docs updated.\n- Known and next: the resource counts behind the verdict are right for the\n  iCE40 flow the pipeline uses. Measured on one design, ECP5 counts miss\n  carry LUTs and DP16KD block RAM, Gowin counts muxes as LUTs and LUT-RAM as\n  block RAM, and the Xilinx script passes synth_xilinx an option it does\n  not have; the next commit corrects the counting per family.\n- The route-policy gate caught GET /api/training/target-profiles (added by\n  9bae8e559) without a policy; it is a public read like the other training\n  catalogues and was already in the training-monitor route table. The\n  operator-status route counts (stale since 352fcc9d0 added seven\n  authenticated fit/cohort job routes) are the measured 149/35/114.\n- Training stream: when the local proxy finished before the manager sealed\n  the record, the stream returned after heartbeats alone, so the browser\n  kept the run \"running\" and warm-start/resume disabled (the live event\n  suite failed about one run in three). With a manager, a finished proxy\n  now waits for the sealed record (30 polls) and then states how it ended;\n  without one, a drained stream still ends silently as before. The suite\n  passed 4/4.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"a60c587726578d4ac5d32028ea0d8007363f5d4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/a60c587726578d4ac5d32028ea0d8007363f5d4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/f995a8523b3a099ac6c6c87b598b8d70f4c6e0af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/f995a8523b3a099ac6c6c87b598b8d70f4c6e0af","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGY5OTVhODUyM2IzYTA5OWFjNmM2Yzg3YjU5OGI4ZDcwZjRjNmUwYWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/ed933ac980d56cc092d40225590ce79ec81b99cd","sha":"ed933ac980d56cc092d40225590ce79ec81b99cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/ed933ac980d56cc092d40225590ce79ec81b99cd"}],"sha":"f995a8523b3a099ac6c6c87b598b8d70f4c6e0af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/f995a8523b3a099ac6c6c87b598b8d70f4c6e0af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/ed933ac980d56cc092d40225590ce79ec81b99cd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:03:37Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T18:03:37Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio-ui): every analysis view is described in its own numbers and tabled; bifurcation keeps the server''s classification\n\n- Non-trace canvases had no description of their own (and until 12fe77248\n  pointed at exports that hold only the trace). viewDescriptions.ts gives\n  f-I, bifurcation, 2-D sweep, sensitivity, STA, frequency response,\n  characterisation, A/B, E-I network, ISI, phase portrait, precision and\n  multi-model one sentence and one table each, read from the result the view\n  draws. The canvas''s accessible name and the Data table both use it, so\n  neither describes the trace while the canvas shows something else.\n- Sentences say only what the result carries: the first measured firing\n  point (not an interpolated threshold), undefined elasticities counted,\n  a sampled extrema sweep \"not a numerical continuation\", the STA as an\n  average of the first state (not of the drive), saturation named. Tables\n  cap at 200 rows and say how many are left out.\n- The analysis-job validator dropped attractor_kinds, variable and protocol\n  from bifurcation results, so no swept point could be called fixed or\n  oscillating; they are validated (known kinds, matching length) and kept.\n- Live e2e: an f-I run names the canvas and tables its points.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"a3ba33f4916b34db8d689f22b8fed94bdf901bed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/a3ba33f4916b34db8d689f22b8fed94bdf901bed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/ed933ac980d56cc092d40225590ce79ec81b99cd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/ed933ac980d56cc092d40225590ce79ec81b99cd","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGVkOTMzYWM5ODBkNTZjYzA5MmQ0MDIyNTU5MGNlNzllYzgxYjk5Y2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/7c88877dcad40bb76593cf933d22bdc7c589839c","sha":"7c88877dcad40bb76593cf933d22bdc7c589839c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/7c88877dcad40bb76593cf933d22bdc7c589839c"}],"sha":"ed933ac980d56cc092d40225590ce79ec81b99cd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/ed933ac980d56cc092d40225590ce79ec81b99cd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/7c88877dcad40bb76593cf933d22bdc7c589839c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:37:55Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:37:55Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio-ui): gating variables readable on their own axis; library names no longer run under badges; Fit and Training forms laid out and legible\n\n- Trace: every state shared one axis labelled mV, so a conductance model''s\n  gates (0-1) lay flat on the zero line under a 100 mV voltage. States whose\n  swing differs from the first state''s by more than 10x get a second panel;\n  axes carry a declared unit or the state names (no catalogue model declares\n  state units, so mV was never true). Stacked panels no longer print their\n  own time ticks into the gap; \"ms\" moved out from under the Data table\n  button.\n- Model library: long names ran under the tier badges; the name now ends in\n  an ellipsis, the badges keep their width, and the row title names the\n  model. Live e2e checks every row.\n- Fit: \"Observed variable\" sat inline after the model radio buttons and\n  read as a third choice; it has its own row with a note.\n- Training: metric charts used 7-8 px text and had no epoch ticks; 11 px,\n  epoch ticks, legend spaced by its text and an accessible summary. Model and\n  Dataset selects span two columns (were cut to \"Spiking networ\"); two native\n  buttons take the Studio''s button style.\n- Training run list: the list endpoint can still say \"running\" after the\n  status route is terminal; it is read until it agrees (bounded).\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"fcd40af98940a49f37d7fd65757f9281056e77ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/fcd40af98940a49f37d7fd65757f9281056e77ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/7c88877dcad40bb76593cf933d22bdc7c589839c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/7c88877dcad40bb76593cf933d22bdc7c589839c","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDdjODg4NzdkY2FkNDBiYjc2NTkzY2Y5MzNkMjJiZGM3YzU4OTgzOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/bdce4fa17ae7641c4d5aadf180244d02b8c70de8","sha":"bdce4fa17ae7641c4d5aadf180244d02b8c70de8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/bdce4fa17ae7641c4d5aadf180244d02b8c70de8"}],"sha":"7c88877dcad40bb76593cf933d22bdc7c589839c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/7c88877dcad40bb76593cf933d22bdc7c589839c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/bdce4fa17ae7641c4d5aadf180244d02b8c70de8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:03:47Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T17:03:47Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio-ui): network canvas draws and connects projections; defaults stay physiological at any dt; pipeline, ODE switch and training list say what is true\n\n- Population nodes rendered no connection handles: no projection was ever\n  drawn (ReactFlow #008 per projection per render) and drag-to-connect had\n  nothing to drag from. Handles enter left, leave right.\n- The canvas fitted one node at 2x and put the next outside the view; it now\n  refits (max 1:1) when a population is added or the canvas is resized.\n  Attribution is no longer hidden (the console warned on every render); it\n  is styled to pass 4.5:1 contrast.\n- Default projection weight was a fixed 40 (reasoned for dt 0.1) with -1x\n  inhibition: every default network ran away (1290 Hz per neuron at the\n  Studio''s dt 0.5, 6340 Hz at 0.1). Now the one-step kick is 0.2 threshold at\n  any dt (w = 4/dt) and inhibition is 4x (Brunel 2000): measured E 27-30 Hz,\n  I 48-52 Hz at dt 0.5/0.1/0.05. A population spiking on half the steps or\n  more is named as saturated instead of reported as a rate.\n- Pipeline -> ICE40 showed only \"...\" on another button for ~80 s; a status\n  line now names the stages.\n- Switching Models/ODE kept showing the other source''s run; it now runs the\n  new source (the guided-flow spec counts that run as its simulation step).\n- The retained-run list was read on the terminal event, before the job\n  record is sealed, and showed a finished run as \"running\".\n- RTL and FPGA views pointed to \"Compile\" and an \"SV button\" that do not\n  exist; RTL, FPGA synthesis, Training and Network canvas have headings.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"968ffe1e3a2faf40c34c4982d7bda3a2ec5243e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/968ffe1e3a2faf40c34c4982d7bda3a2ec5243e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/bdce4fa17ae7641c4d5aadf180244d02b8c70de8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/bdce4fa17ae7641c4d5aadf180244d02b8c70de8","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGJkY2U0ZmExN2FlNzY0MWM0ZDVhYWRmMTgwMjQ0ZDAyYjhjNzBkZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/12fe77248ad7ec7005a62c5e98be8a48d698621b","sha":"12fe77248ad7ec7005a62c5e98be8a48d698621b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/12fe77248ad7ec7005a62c5e98be8a48d698621b"}],"sha":"bdce4fa17ae7641c4d5aadf180244d02b8c70de8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/bdce4fa17ae7641c4d5aadf180244d02b8c70de8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/12fe77248ad7ec7005a62c5e98be8a48d698621b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:37:50Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:37:50Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio-ui): multi-model overlay offers every model and states its drive; plot names stop pointing at exports that lack them\n\n- Non-trace plot canvases were named \"Its values are in the CSV and JSON\n  exports\"; those exports hold the trace run only. The sentence now says\n  so; the multi-model view describes itself in numbers.\n- Multi-model picker listed models.slice(0, 50): 135 of 185 models could\n  not be overlaid. Every model is offered, with a filter; the panel is\n  titled like the view its empty state points to.\n- The overlay says which drive every model had and that the current is\n  read in each model''s own units; legend entries name the state drawn and\n  wrap instead of overlapping every 120 px.\n- Spike statistics labelled the CV with thresholds of their own\n  (\"bursting\") while the classifier called the same run \"chaotic\"; the\n  panel now shows the number only, the classifier names the pattern.\n- The trace''s drive axis claimed nA for every model; no model declares\n  its drive unit, so it says \"I (model''s own units)\".\n- AstrocyteModel and AstrocyteNeuron both read \"Astrocyte\" in the library;\n  short labels are kept only where unique.\n- A/B section titled \"A/B compare\" with a \"Run A/B\" button (was \"vs\").\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"48e2df4dc5e04158a577d3ae2c9b28a5cf25622c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/48e2df4dc5e04158a577d3ae2c9b28a5cf25622c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/12fe77248ad7ec7005a62c5e98be8a48d698621b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/12fe77248ad7ec7005a62c5e98be8a48d698621b","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDEyZmU3NzI0OGFkN2VjNzAwNWE2MmM1ZTk4YmU4YTQ4ZDY5ODYyMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/383624cbaf9f22ff6591ec8812dbf26bdf70307c","sha":"383624cbaf9f22ff6591ec8812dbf26bdf70307c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/383624cbaf9f22ff6591ec8812dbf26bdf70307c"}],"sha":"12fe77248ad7ec7005a62c5e98be8a48d698621b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/12fe77248ad7ec7005a62c5e98be8a48d698621b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/383624cbaf9f22ff6591ec8812dbf26bdf70307c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:37:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T15:37:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): clock macro-stepping models by their macro step\n\nHodgkin-Huxley, Connor-Stevens and Wang-Buzsaki advance a fixed macro step\nper step() call (1 ms of 100 x 0.01 ms; 0.5 ms of 50), as their profiles\ndeclare in numerical.macro_step. The Studio timed every call as one dt:\na 100 ms Hodgkin-Huxley request ran 10 s of model time and reported\n6330 Hz (now 60 Hz); Wang-Buzsaki at 10 uA/cm2 reported 14 280 Hz in the\nA/B view (now 290 Hz). Time axes, rates, analyses, exports and the\nanalysis budget (over-projected 100x) all inherited the error.\n\n- ModelRunInputs.step_ms = simulated time of one call; the run clock,\n  drive trace, step count, failure times, response dt, receipt and\n  experiment numerical block use it. The receipt keeps dt (the sub-step).\n- Another dt is refused for these models: the class picks its own\n  sub-step count from dt and nothing declares a call''s length then.\n  Tests that used \"Hodgkin-Huxley at dt 0.05\" as their non-default-dt\n  vehicle (whose results were 20x mistimed) now use AdEx.\n- A macro-stepping model cannot form a network population (the graph\n  advances every population once per dt) and is not offered to the canvas.\n- Model detail carries macro_step; the dt control shows the fixed sub-step\n  and the macro step instead of a slider the server would refuse.\n- Exported scripts print \"N steps of X ms\", not \"at dt X ms\".\n\nModel files are untouched (source hashes are pinned by benchmark gates).\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"e9ddb1edbfafc11f4fcd02b953c6a70d8ba717eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/e9ddb1edbfafc11f4fcd02b953c6a70d8ba717eb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/383624cbaf9f22ff6591ec8812dbf26bdf70307c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/383624cbaf9f22ff6591ec8812dbf26bdf70307c","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDM4MzYyNGNiYWY5ZjIyZmY2NTkxZWM4ODEyZGJmMjZiZGY3MDMwN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/b1fba2604fc70289ebb3084ed0a667b330859bb3","sha":"b1fba2604fc70289ebb3084ed0a667b330859bb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/b1fba2604fc70289ebb3084ed0a667b330859bb3"}],"sha":"383624cbaf9f22ff6591ec8812dbf26bdf70307c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/383624cbaf9f22ff6591ec8812dbf26bdf70307c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/b1fba2604fc70289ebb3084ed0a667b330859bb3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:36:37Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:36:37Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): sweeps run the chosen drive; failures are said in words\n\nFound by pressing every view''s action live (the lesson of f08b1a4cd).\n\nBifurcation: BifurcationRequest had no protocol field, so the protocol the\nStudio sends was silently dropped and every point ran under a sine drive\n(hard-coded since May). For the default catalogue model (ATypeKNeuron)\nthe sine''s negative half-cycle leaves the model''s safety bounds at\nt = 62.4 ms for any swept value and any dt (measured at dt 0.5, 0.1, 0.05),\nso the bifurcation view failed every time. Bifurcation and heatmap\nrequests now carry protocol/frequency_hz (default constant), the job and\nsynchronous routes use them, and results state the drive (_drive_fields).\nSensitivity and characterisation keep their constant drive by definition;\nthe frequency response keeps its mean-zero sine (open question recorded).\n\nFailures: a 422 model_simulation_failed detail is rendered in full (model,\nbackend, step, time, diagnostic) instead of its code; an analysis job''s\nexception class (ModelSimulationFailure) gets a sentence, the code kept as\ndata-error-code; the error banner has Dismiss (panel jobs deliberately do\nnot clear store-owned errors, so it outlived its view).\n\nCharacterisation: the progress socket had no open timeout; through a\ndevelopment proxy that did not forward /ws the run sat at \"Starting\ncharacterisation... 0%\" until the browser gave up on the handshake. It now\nfalls back to HTTP after 5 s, and vite dev/preview forward /ws (the API\nstill enforces its origin allow-list).\n\nTests: tests/test_studio_analysis_sweep_drive.py (5, incl. sine -> 422 with\nthe safety-bounds diagnostic and unknown protocol refused), 72 existing\nsweep tests, two socket-timeout store tests, error-sentence tests.\nmypy strict, tsc, eslint, vitest 1311; browser runs default 14, graph 27.\nLive: characterize, f-I, sensitivity, bifurcation, 2-D sweep, STA, code,\ndelays and E-I all produce results for the default model.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"808d2edb3dd36889e58be47e27c09dd16cf8eaf0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/808d2edb3dd36889e58be47e27c09dd16cf8eaf0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/b1fba2604fc70289ebb3084ed0a667b330859bb3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/b1fba2604fc70289ebb3084ed0a667b330859bb3","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGIxZmJhMjYwNGZjNzAyODllYmIzMDg0ZWQwYTY2N2IzMzA4NTliYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/0dc870a4fddcd47924d15a30ab8bdd51b1a04a51","sha":"0dc870a4fddcd47924d15a30ab8bdd51b1a04a51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/0dc870a4fddcd47924d15a30ab8bdd51b1a04a51"}],"sha":"b1fba2604fc70289ebb3084ed0a667b330859bb3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/b1fba2604fc70289ebb3084ed0a667b330859bb3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/0dc870a4fddcd47924d15a30ab8bdd51b1a04a51/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:37:37Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:37:37Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio-ui): keyboard and screen-reader access, honest workbench actions\n\nPhase 4 of the live UI audit.\n\nKeyboard: a model was chosen by clicking a div, so no model could be\nchosen without a pointer. Model rows (list/listitem, the name a button\nwith aria-current), saved sessions, experiment presets, behaviour filter\nchips (aria-pressed), onboarding step dots, the ISI shortcut and the code\none-liner are real buttons; a scan for pointer-only handlers on div/span\nnow finds only the keyboard help''s backdrop (Escape closes it; the dialog\nitself has role and name).\n\nNames: model search, current protocol, model B, FPGA target and the E-I\nsliders; the 133 \"DOI\" links name their model; left-panel sections are h2.\nDead links: every capability \"docs\" link and the unavailable panel''s\n\"Documentation\" link pointed at /<repo path> on the Studio server (404 on\nboth servers); publishedDocsUrl maps them to the MkDocs site (7 pages\nchecked live, 200), and a test ties the site to mkdocs.yml and requires\neach declared page to exist.\n\nWorkbench: \"Save project\" and \"Open projects\" and \"Browse models\"/\"Edit\nequations\" all switched the view to the trace. They now save (via the new\ndialog), show the project list and focus the model search or equations.\n\nTextPromptDialog (native dialog, showModal, labelled field, multi-line for\na trace) replaces window.prompt for save project, save session and import\ntrace; six browser specs now fill it, the canvas one by keyboard. A banner\nwith Retry replaces the tooltip-only \"capability check failed\". index.html\npaints dark with a loading line. Layout: model rows show state/param\ncounts instead of a comma-joined list that could not wrap, slider values\ngrow with their unit and sliders may shrink, the admin identity form\nwraps, admin status words and metrics are no longer truncated.\n\nAudit before -> after this phase: unnamed control kinds 16 -> 0 on 23\nviews, overflow kinds 3 -> 0, views with a heading 5 -> 23; no console\nerror, no contrast failure. tsc, eslint, vitest 1304; browser runs\ndefault 14, graph 27, live 7, event 1.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"b8f897e0a007312b98baf7fc6c075ab858377164","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/b8f897e0a007312b98baf7fc6c075ab858377164"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/0dc870a4fddcd47924d15a30ab8bdd51b1a04a51","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/0dc870a4fddcd47924d15a30ab8bdd51b1a04a51","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDBkYzg3MGE0ZmRkY2Q0NzkyNGQxNWEzMGFiOGJkZDUxYjFhMDRhNTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/f08b1a4cdc2be8a92325cb233fb1c09d43844107","sha":"f08b1a4cdc2be8a92325cb233fb1c09d43844107","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/f08b1a4cdc2be8a92325cb233fb1c09d43844107"}],"sha":"0dc870a4fddcd47924d15a30ab8bdd51b1a04a51","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/0dc870a4fddcd47924d15a30ab8bdd51b1a04a51"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/f08b1a4cdc2be8a92325cb233fb1c09d43844107/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:16:05Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:16:05Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): the E-I network fires; it is now the Brunel-style model it claims\n\nFound while checking the new empty state live: the E-I network view ran\nand showed no spike. Measured on both implementations (Rust engine and\nNumPy fallback, which agreed): zero spikes for every external rate the\n0.1-100 Hz slider reaches, at any duration; activity began near 1,000 Hz,\nwhich is the drive the engine''s own tests used (5,000 Hz).\n\nCauses, both implementations: every delta-synapse jump was multiplied by\nthe step size, so a spike moved the membrane by weight x dt (0.01 mV for\nthe default E-to-E weight at dt = 0.1 ms, and a result that changed with\ndt); and each neuron had one external Poisson input. Now: weights are\nmembrane jumps in mV delivered one step later, and every neuron receives\n800 external excitatory Poisson inputs of 0.1 mV at ext_rate each\n(Brunel 2000), so the drive reaches threshold at 15 / (0.1 x 800 x 20 ms)\n= 9.4 Hz. Default ext_rate 12 Hz: about 29-31 Hz with the default g = 4\nweights, whose recurrent excitation and inhibition cancel on average.\n\nAlso fixed on the way: mean_exc_rate/mean_inh_rate averaged only the rate\nbins that held a spike (overstating sparse activity); they now count\nsilent time. The engine''s Knuth Poisson loop never terminated once\nexp(-mean) underflowed; it uses rand_distr''s exact sampler. The route\nbounds ext_rate to 0-1000 Hz. The Studio''s E->I and I->E sliders were\nswapped against the model''s post-pre names (w_ei is I->E); relabelled,\nnamed for screen readers with units, and a note states the threshold rate.\n\nTests: 6 Rust unit tests (default drive fires, sub-threshold silence,\ndt independence, mean rate counts silent time, huge mean terminates),\ntests/test_studio_ei_network_model.py on both implementations (16), a\nno-op assertion (n_spikes >= 0) replaced by a real one, binding goldens\nre-derived at the default drive (70 spikes = 57 E + 13 I). 45 E-I and\nStudio network tests pass on the rebuilt engine; rustfmt clean on the\nchanged files; cargo clippy not run locally (it rebuilds bundled Z3).\nLive: default network 578 spikes, E 28.8 Hz, I 29.2 Hz.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"49db6f50879a827f5e8bec96b04388abc0870fbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/49db6f50879a827f5e8bec96b04388abc0870fbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/f08b1a4cdc2be8a92325cb233fb1c09d43844107","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/f08b1a4cdc2be8a92325cb233fb1c09d43844107","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGYwOGIxYTRjZGMyYmU4YTkyMzI1Y2IyMzNmYjFjMDlkNDM4NDQxMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/a5417c909adc71edfc902679de9e1e06e4b5678c","sha":"a5417c909adc71edfc902679de9e1e06e4b5678c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/a5417c909adc71edfc902679de9e1e06e4b5678c"}],"sha":"f08b1a4cdc2be8a92325cb233fb1c09d43844107","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/f08b1a4cdc2be8a92325cb233fb1c09d43844107"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/a5417c909adc71edfc902679de9e1e06e4b5678c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:30:29Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:30:29Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio-ui): empty plot views say so instead of showing the trace\n\nThe live audit found eleven plot views (2-D sweep, bifurcation,\nsensitivity, f-I curve, STA, frequency response, characterization,\nmulti-model, A/B compare, Q8.8 precision, E-I network) that, with no\nresult of their own, drew the membrane trace under their own tab; a\nscreen reader was given the trace''s description. SimulationPlot now asks\nviewEmptyState for the view''s empty state: a heading, what produces the\nresult (naming the sweep parameters still missing, or why an STA or ISI\ncannot be formed from this run), and the action button that fills it\nwhere one exists, named as in the header. Every plot view gets an h2.\n\nPanel titles and view-switcher labels now come from one table\n(PANEL_TITLES), so a view has one name in the switcher, its heading, its\nempty state and its unavailable notice.\n\nChecks: tsc, eslint, vitest 1299; browser runs default 13, graph 27,\nlive 7 passed; the empty E-I view''s button was clicked live and filled\nthe view.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"b36a5f32dcdb3b9cd334eeffaa55e08427efb1d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/b36a5f32dcdb3b9cd334eeffaa55e08427efb1d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/a5417c909adc71edfc902679de9e1e06e4b5678c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/a5417c909adc71edfc902679de9e1e06e4b5678c","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGE1NDE3YzkwOWFkYzcxZWRmYzkwMjY3OWRlOWUxZTA2ZTRiNTY3OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/420ba8563d5f373aff6fdb368b4ae6874a065bea","sha":"420ba8563d5f373aff6fdb368b4ae6874a065bea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/420ba8563d5f373aff6fdb368b4ae6874a065bea"}],"sha":"a5417c909adc71edfc902679de9e1e06e4b5678c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/a5417c909adc71edfc902679de9e1e06e4b5678c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/420ba8563d5f373aff6fdb368b4ae6874a065bea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:06:26Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:06:26Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"docs: regenerate the API reference for the Studio DCLS docstrings\n\nfc8070ce5 reworded two docstrings (the DCLS backend probe and the local\nbenchmark) and was committed without regenerating docs/API_REFERENCE.md,\nso generate_docs --check reported it stale. Regenerated, no other change.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"a3b03aaf639548219221317e70549f200d2a06d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/a3b03aaf639548219221317e70549f200d2a06d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/420ba8563d5f373aff6fdb368b4ae6874a065bea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/420ba8563d5f373aff6fdb368b4ae6874a065bea","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDQyMGJhODU2M2Q1ZjM3M2FmZjZmZGIzNjhiNGFlNjg3NGEwNjViZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/b99467b897ca3f835353e4c87fb2f9fce15c02f5","sha":"b99467b897ca3f835353e4c87fb2f9fce15c02f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/b99467b897ca3f835353e4c87fb2f9fce15c02f5"}],"sha":"420ba8563d5f373aff6fdb368b4ae6874a065bea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/420ba8563d5f373aff6fdb368b4ae6874a065bea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/b99467b897ca3f835353e4c87fb2f9fce15c02f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:05:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:05:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"feat(studio-ui): a navigable header and a real view switcher\n\nThe live UI audit found one wrapping header row of about forty controls:\nabbreviated view buttons with nothing saying which view was showing, four\nviews repeated as same-named buttons, sweep selects named only by a\ncapability tooltip, and raw refusal identifiers shown as explanations.\n\nThe header now has three rows. The first holds the title, the capability\nstatus, the Models/ODE switch (buttons with aria-pressed) and sign-in. The\nsecond holds the actions in named groups with verb names (Characterize,\nMeasure frequency response, Compute STA, Run E-I network, Generate code,\nGenerate RTL, Build IR, Emit SystemVerilog) and three visual weights\ninstead of one colour per button; the sweep selects have visible labels.\nThe third is ViewTabs: one tablist, full names in five groups, the\nselected view announced and underlined, roving tabindex, arrow keys, Home\nand End (WAI-ARIA tabs pattern), and the view area as its tabpanel and the\npage''s main landmark. RTL and FPGA synthesis are listed in both modes.\nA refused analysis request is explained in a sentence; the identifier\nstays as data-error-code.\n\nAlso fixed: at phone width the header covered most of the screen and the\npage title was display:none (removing the only h1 from the accessibility\ntree); the switcher overhung the page at 200 % zoom. The three live\ntraining specs added with the train-to-hardware chain ran in the mocked\ndefault e2e run (run in CI) and failed there every time; they are now\nexcluded, and a unit test requires every live spec to be excluded from the\nmocked run and matched by a live config (it reports those three against\nthe previous config). Studio docs, tutorials and the keyboard help name\nthe new controls; a typed catalogue count became a bound count.\n\nChecks: tsc, eslint, 1289 unit tests; browser runs default 13, graph 27\n(contrast baseline and 200 % zoom included), live 7, event 1 passed.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"eb1d6072192f325c5a018b35c070fb32e2c99e4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/eb1d6072192f325c5a018b35c070fb32e2c99e4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/b99467b897ca3f835353e4c87fb2f9fce15c02f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/b99467b897ca3f835353e4c87fb2f9fce15c02f5","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGI5OTQ2N2I4OTdjYTNmODM1MzUzZTRjODdmYjJmOWZjZTE1YzAyZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/55608e1ff32b127ded4dadc0a4f64a88fc50a997","sha":"55608e1ff32b127ded4dadc0a4f64a88fc50a997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/55608e1ff32b127ded4dadc0a4f64a88fc50a997"}],"sha":"b99467b897ca3f835353e4c87fb2f9fce15c02f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/b99467b897ca3f835353e4c87fb2f9fce15c02f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/55608e1ff32b127ded4dadc0a4f64a88fc50a997/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:36:17Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:36:17Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio-ui): a readable type scale and themed form controls\n\nA live audit of all 21 Studio views (Chromium, real backend) found most\ntext set at 8 to 10 px: 17,000 text nodes at 8 px, 6,500 at 9 px and\n11,000 at 10 px. The Studio now has a type scale in index.css with a\nfloor of 11 px for dense metadata (--fs-meta), 12 px for body text\n(--fs-body) and 13 px for primary controls (--fs-ui). Inline sizes in\n42 components moved onto the tokens, `small` no longer shrinks below the\nfloor, and the plots draw their axis labels at 11 px.\n\n`color-scheme: dark` and zero-specificity base rules give text fields,\ntext areas, file pickers, checkboxes, radios and fieldsets the Studio\npalette; the fitting laboratory, training monitor and candidate editor\nshowed white browser defaults. The focus ring now covers every input\ntype, select, link and disclosure summary instead of three input types.\n\nChecks: tsc, eslint, 1274 unit tests, and the live graph e2e suite\n(27 passed, including the contrast baseline and the 200 % zoom check).\nNo contrast pair regressed.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"04c8f27c13def9d69f7ab0151350bf69ad50edaa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/04c8f27c13def9d69f7ab0151350bf69ad50edaa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/55608e1ff32b127ded4dadc0a4f64a88fc50a997","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/55608e1ff32b127ded4dadc0a4f64a88fc50a997","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDU1NjA4ZTFmZjMyYjEyN2RlZDRkYWRjMGE0ZjY0YTg4ZmM1MGE5OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/fc8070ce58e5a936193d325f036055cc60e9e2d2","sha":"fc8070ce58e5a936193d325f036055cc60e9e2d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/fc8070ce58e5a936193d325f036055cc60e9e2d2"}],"sha":"55608e1ff32b127ded4dadc0a4f64a88fc50a997","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/55608e1ff32b127ded4dadc0a4f64a88fc50a997"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/fc8070ce58e5a936193d325f036055cc60e9e2d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:29:34Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T09:29:34Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): never run Julia in the API process; the Delays view froze the server\n\nThe Delays view requests the DCLS kernel information and the parity\nevaluation at the same time. In a server process that had not loaded\nPyTorch yet, both probed the Julia backend from separate request threads.\nJuliaCall work that compiles or reads a source file only completes on the\nthread that initialised Julia; issued from another thread it held the GIL\nand waited forever, so every route stopped answering, /api/health included.\nFound in the live Studio UI audit; stacks captured with faulthandler.\n\nThe Studio server now declares Julia for the DCLS kernel but never runs it\nin its own process (IN_PROCESS_REFUSED_BACKENDS), which it already did\nwhenever PyTorch was loaded; the UI shows it as parity verified offline and\nthe offline parity suite keeps covering it. A new test sends the view''s\nfour requests concurrently to a fresh server process and requires every\nanswer and /api/health without JuliaCall ever being imported; against the\nprevious source the same script hangs inside the Julia load.\n\nThe underlying library defect (every lazily loaded Julia kernel is unsafe\nfrom a non-initialising thread) is recorded as open catalogue-phase work:\nfixing it touches files bound by benchmark evidence.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"562ff03327d1e355b45639f9faacab815378cfed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/562ff03327d1e355b45639f9faacab815378cfed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/fc8070ce58e5a936193d325f036055cc60e9e2d2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/fc8070ce58e5a936193d325f036055cc60e9e2d2","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGZjODA3MGNlNThlNWE5MzYxOTNkMzI1ZjAzNjA1NWNjNjBlOWUyZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/889bc370d0a52117c6f83ce487c797b387b77b3c","sha":"889bc370d0a52117c6f83ce487c797b387b77b3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/889bc370d0a52117c6f83ce487c797b387b77b3c"}],"sha":"fc8070ce58e5a936193d325f036055cc60e9e2d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/fc8070ce58e5a936193d325f036055cc60e9e2d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/889bc370d0a52117c6f83ce487c797b387b77b3c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:36:08Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T08:36:08Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"docs: bind public formal counts and fidelity evidence to what is committed\n\nFormal counts. The git-tracked hdl/formal inventory is 90 proof jobs and\n447 statements (296 assert, 115 assume, 36 cover). The README diagram\nsaid 61 jobs, the formal-verification tutorial''s table said 293/112/441,\nand FOR_RESEARCH_LABS, bci_codec and tutorials 32, 52 and 60 said 18 jobs\nand 130 statements; the v3.13 report presented 18/130 as the current\ninventory and now points to the README instead. The existing test checked\nthree named pages, so the others drifted unseen. A new test scans every\npublic page (dated changelogs excluded) for job, statement, breakdown and\ncatalogue/non-catalogue counts; on the previous tree it reports all 20\nstale claims.\n\nFidelity evidence. 31 polyglot-complete rows named `this commit` as their\nevidence. Each now names its committed benchmark result, receipt, trace or\nformal job; every file was checked to belong to its model. A new test\nrequires every evidence cell to name a tracked file (or, for runtime\nclosures, an existing commit); on the previous tree it reports the 31\nplaceholders. The COBA LIF pages still described the formal job as a\ngenerated depth-4 reset-safety check; since bc0195bcc it is a curated\ndepth-8 job with reset, first-event and refractory assertions, recorded\nas passing there.\n\nThe remaining uncommitted Model 29 (COBA LIF reclosure) work is parked,\nnot landed, at refs/archive/wip/model29-coba-lif-2026-09-29 by owner\ndecision: it resumes with the catalogue work.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"5c89c2ee561c8cfe6311469373bfc90c64dab935","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/5c89c2ee561c8cfe6311469373bfc90c64dab935"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/889bc370d0a52117c6f83ce487c797b387b77b3c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/889bc370d0a52117c6f83ce487c797b387b77b3c","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDg4OWJjMzcwZDBhNTIxMTdjNmY4M2NlNDg3Yzc5N2IzODdiNzdiM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/3763fff65232d09252b9650743feb7a1a6cc3b30","sha":"3763fff65232d09252b9650743feb7a1a6cc3b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/3763fff65232d09252b9650743feb7a1a6cc3b30"}],"sha":"889bc370d0a52117c6f83ce487c797b387b77b3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/889bc370d0a52117c6f83ce487c797b387b77b3c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/3763fff65232d09252b9650743feb7a1a6cc3b30/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:53:37Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T07:53:37Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"test(studio): land the verified evidence gates and storage record reads\n\nTake over the parts of the long-standing Studio working-tree changes that\nhold: the exact-coverage CI steps for the evidence input limits and the\nevidence process (both at 100 % branch locally), docstring-policy entries for\nsixteen storage and API modules, and real tests for laboratory-route record\nreads (another owner''s record is reported absent; the owner''s fit is\nreturned). Three further storage gates are not added: storage_peer''s kernel\nrace branches, the distinct-UID endpoint read and a third-party-owned\nancestor cannot be reached in a single-user runner without stubs.\n\nThe reload-guard notes no longer name a CI worker setting that CI does not use.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"180d3628558a396e340f7b20df111bce227c589d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/180d3628558a396e340f7b20df111bce227c589d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/3763fff65232d09252b9650743feb7a1a6cc3b30","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/3763fff65232d09252b9650743feb7a1a6cc3b30","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDM3NjNmZmY2NTIzMmQwOTI1MmI5NjUwNzQzZmViN2ExYTZjYzNiMzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/9bae8e559dbb8deb21d58e4ae17982c1e0d2a9fe","sha":"9bae8e559dbb8deb21d58e4ae17982c1e0d2a9fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/9bae8e559dbb8deb21d58e4ae17982c1e0d2a9fe"}],"sha":"3763fff65232d09252b9650743feb7a1a6cc3b30","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/3763fff65232d09252b9650743feb7a1a6cc3b30"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/9bae8e559dbb8deb21d58e4ae17982c1e0d2a9fe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T05:18:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T05:18:49Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"feat(st23): train-to-hardware chain with measured conversion and target evidence\n\nEvent datasets to Studio training: manifests of local N-MNIST, SHD and\nDVS-CIFAR10 recordings, whole-group splits and declared encoders form an event\ncontract that is verified, budgeted and stored with the job; native N-MNIST,\nSHD and DVS readers in Rust, Go, Julia and Mojo refuse rather than fall back.\n\nANN-to-SNN conversion lowers the model''s actual forward invocations, keeps\ntrained biases, a signed linear readout and per-call ReLU/QCFS scales, and\nreplays under one float64 profile in NumPy, Rust, Go, Mojo and Julia with a\nsource-bound measured dispatch order and an installed comparison command.\nQCFS evaluates torch-free in all five runtimes with bit parity; conversion\nrestores accelerator generators too.\n\nMeasured evidence: preregistered training criteria (API, `sc-neurocore train`,\nTraining Monitor); a QCFS conversion route judged on the converted network with\na sealed loss report; fixed-point target calibration against registered\nprofiles; a hardware experiment protocol and recomputable receipt that never\ninfers energy from operation counts. `sc-neurocore deploy` now exports the\ncheckpoint''s converted network instead of discarding it.\n\nFixes: event-job record reads re-validated whole manifests (275 ms per read);\nweight fingerprint for hidden []; training and CLI architecture guards; stale\ndocs examples. Physical target execution remains open.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: b9f0","tree":{"sha":"42cad90e1a5e0546ef1707fde562293c414db2cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/42cad90e1a5e0546ef1707fde562293c414db2cb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/9bae8e559dbb8deb21d58e4ae17982c1e0d2a9fe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"http