6,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/29a29f757413a5b976ca5450355ef60d25ce87c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T00:43:38Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T00:43:38Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): bound embedded workers before task loading\n\nApply POSIX data, CPU, descriptor, file-size and core-dump ceilings to each\nembedded worker after supervisor registration and before payload or task import.\nNested EDA children retain the inherited hard ceiling, so their own configured\nlimits cannot cause a worker-start failure. Real process tests prove refusal,\nthe import boundary and normal Yosys execution.\n\nParity: Python Studio worker only; no polyglot counterpart.\nBenchmarks: not applicable; no compute kernel or benchmarked path changed.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: 7e4a1","tree":{"sha":"2256da1d69bac61519486ec4680f1a1e6d5cce68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/2256da1d69bac61519486ec4680f1a1e6d5cce68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/29a29f757413a5b976ca5450355ef60d25ce87c8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/29a29f757413a5b976ca5450355ef60d25ce87c8","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKDI5YTI5Zjc1NzQxM2E1Yjk3NmNhNTQ1MDM1NWVmNjBkMjVjZTg3Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/b7d8a0fc2bdb57815e98587339b61bab69852573","sha":"b7d8a0fc2bdb57815e98587339b61bab69852573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/b7d8a0fc2bdb57815e98587339b61bab69852573"}],"sha":"29a29f757413a5b976ca5450355ef60d25ce87c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/29a29f757413a5b976ca5450355ef60d25ce87c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/b7d8a0fc2bdb57815e98587339b61bab69852573/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:24:07Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T14:24:07Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"test(studio): cover a process that exits between the /proc listing and its probe\n\nThe jobs exact-coverage step failed at 99 % on lines 53-54 of\njobs_process_state.group_survivors. That branch handles a process that\nappears in the /proc listing and has exited by the time its group is read.\nUntil now a test reached it only when some unrelated process happened to\nexit during a scan, so the gate passed or failed by chance.\n\nThe new test makes the listing stale by naming a process id that does not\nexist. The real getpgid call then refuses it, exactly as it does after such\nan exit, and the scan reports no survivor.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: 52ae","tree":{"sha":"3f40c2cb9c3dc34104f8c271713581400c9b2563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/3f40c2cb9c3dc34104f8c271713581400c9b2563"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/b7d8a0fc2bdb57815e98587339b61bab69852573","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/b7d8a0fc2bdb57815e98587339b61bab69852573","node_id":"C_kwDORM9tGtoAKGI3ZDhhMGZjMmJkYjU3ODE1ZTk4NTg3MzM5YjYxYmFiNjk4NTI1NzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/sc-neurocore/commit/4f22c532fd4016a53c907210e45cb35b9525ed9a","sha":"4f22c532fd4016a53c907210e45cb35b9525ed9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/4f22c532fd4016a53c907210e45cb35b9525ed9a"}],"sha":"b7d8a0fc2bdb57815e98587339b61bab69852573","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/b7d8a0fc2bdb57815e98587339b61bab69852573"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/commits/4f22c532fd4016a53c907210e45cb35b9525ed9a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T11:51:53Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T11:51:53Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(studio): an MNIST training run no longer trains on synthetic data\n\nWhen torchvision was not installed, the MNIST loader returned the synthetic\ndemonstration data instead. The run then trained on 64 random features and\nrecorded itself as an MNIST run: the configuration event, the resolved\nconfiguration and the job all said \"mnist\". The only visible sign was an\ninput width of 64 in the architecture string.\n\nThe loader now fails with the reason, which says that no other data was\nsubstituted. The training job records it as its error and in its failed\nstatus artefact, and writes no weight checkpoint. The test that asserted the\nsubstitution now asserts the refusal. torchvision is made absent through\nsys.modules, because it cannot be uninstalled from a shared environment.\nThe training monitor page described the substitution as a feature and now\nstates the refusal.\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)\nSeat: 52ae","tree":{"sha":"c0977dee87c3b1f0d75146d875d1f8067b695cc6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/trees/c0977dee87c3b1f0d75146d875d1f8067b695cc6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/sc-neurocore/git/commits/4f22c532fd4016a53c907210e45cb35b9525ed9a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://