ib","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Zakarialabib/Rust-Phoenix-Android-Tools/commits/96ee6a82b4c6f30a43fa321137cbc3ae5ce6297b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-16T22:46:43Z","email":"58374576+Zakarialabib@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Zakarialabib"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-16T22:46:43Z","email":"58374576+Zakarialabib@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Zakarialabib"},"message":"🔒 [security fix] Handle potential panics from unwrap/expect\n\nRefactored Tauri initialization and library helper functions to use proper\nResult-based error handling instead of panicking with unwrap() or expect().\nThis prevents potential Denial of Service (DoS) and improves application\nresilience.\n\nKey changes:\n- Updated tauri::run to return Result and handled it in main.rs.\n- Refactored LazyLock<Regex> to be fallible in flash.rs and flash_rockchip.rs.\n- Removed panicking Default implementation for TemplateEngine.\n- Ensured security checks in flash.rs propagate errors instead of failing open.","tree":{"sha":"0b89315152a800561d8214069e06919f6b68c29e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Zakarialabib/Rust-Phoenix-Android-Tools/git/trees/0b89315152a800561d8214069e06919f6b68c29e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Zakarialabib/Rust-Phoenix-Android-Tools/git/commits/96ee6a82b4c6f30a43fa321137cbc3ae5ce6297b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58374576?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Zakarialabib","id":58374576,"login":"Zakarialabib","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU4Mzc0NTc2"