,"site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Zakarialabib/Rust-Phoenix-Android-Tools/commits/9db3be38fe1f3ef43842d7adb3dc9bc6fb039f11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-01T23:56:36Z","email":"58374576+Zakarialabib@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Zakarialabib"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-01T23:56:36Z","email":"58374576+Zakarialabib@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Zakarialabib"},"message":"security: fix insufficient path sanitization in Amlogic image extraction\n\nImplement a robust `sanitize_filename` helper to prevent path traversal\nattacks using malicious partition or key names. The fix uses a whitelist\napproach and neutralizes directory traversal sequences like ''..''.\n\n🎯 What: Insufficient path sanitization in `flash_amlogic.rs`.\n⚠️ Risk: Potential path traversal allowing arbitrary file creation/overwrite.\n🛡️ Solution: Applied whitelist-based filename sanitization to all file\ncreation sites using untrusted names.","tree":{"sha":"fbc7af264b39a33eae15c8379b4b471d2d5b5866","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Zakarialabib/Rust-Phoenix-Android-Tools/git/trees/fbc7af264b39a33eae15c8379b4b471d2d5b5866"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Zakarialabib/Rust-Phoenix-Android-Tools/git/commits/9db3be38fe1f3ef43842d7adb3dc9bc6fb039f11","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/58374576?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zakarialabib/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.gi