ithub.com/fski/flowlens/commit/83dfb6608a2604e93b48d4e20b2c04169bd95ecb","sha":"83dfb6608a2604e93b48d4e20b2c04169bd95ecb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fski/flowlens/commits/83dfb6608a2604e93b48d4e20b2c04169bd95ecb"}],"sha":"8bdfc1f374f65ba2d4aa3e0596af81220885d5a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fski/flowlens/commits/8bdfc1f374f65ba2d4aa3e0596af81220885d5a4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fski/flowlens/commits/83dfb6608a2604e93b48d4e20b2c04169bd95ecb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T11:35:10Z","email":"fski@tekhne.tail1f1dd6.ts.net","name":"Piotr Fijalkowski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T11:35:10Z","email":"fski@tekhne.tail1f1dd6.ts.net","name":"Piotr Fijalkowski"},"message":"fix(flow): recorder policy-block is loud, not a silent ''cancelled'' (6.4.1)\n\ngetDisplayMedia''s NotAllowedError covers both user-dismissed-picker AND\npermissions-policy blocks (the DevTools panel is an iframe inside devtools://\nwhose embedder policy may forbid display-capture). start() collapsed every\nerror into ''cancelled'', which the UI treats as a silent no-op — a policy-\nblocked recorder was indistinguishable from the user changing their mind.\n\n- classifyDisplayMediaError (pure, tested): blocked / cancelled / failed by\n  error name + message sniff; start() returns reason + errorName/Message.\n- Stop-gap UI: ''Recording blocked in the DevTools panel (display-capture\n  policy)'' toast + console detail. If Piotr''s manual test hits it, next step\n  is the popup-recorder fallback (top-level extension window, where a live\n  probe confirmed getDisplayMedia+MediaRecorder work end-to-end).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"09cae48227b59c9f289af19338caa0ccbfba5365","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fski/flowlens/git/trees/09cae48227b59c9f289af19338caa0ccbfba5365"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/fski/flowlens/git/commits/83dfb6608a2604e93b48d4e20b2c04169bd95ecb",